WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.966
Now what changes, starting
with the platform:

2
00:00:02.966 --> 00:00:07.537
one place where every decision is
written down, signed and replayable.

3
00:00:07.537 --> 00:00:12.468
The book's reference design runs
every analysis, plan, delivery and

4
00:00:12.468 --> 00:00:17.937
evidence step on one Windows Server
2025 host, with a standby for recovery.

5
00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:21.601
The property that matters is
a single authoritative writer:

6
00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.213
two writers would diverge.

7
00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:26.512
Every change is a signed
commit, never a portal click.

8
00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:29.874
It's built from standard
components; it isn't a product.

9
00:00:29.874 --> 00:00:32.112
Two design rules matter at this level.

10
00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:35.487
First, governance and execution never mix.

11
00:00:35.487 --> 00:00:37.878
The governance layer validates plans,

12
00:00:37.878 --> 00:00:41.837
signs them and writes the audit
trail, but never touches a target.

13
00:00:41.837 --> 00:00:45.949
The execution layer runs authorized
plans and decides nothing.

14
00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:48.156
They run under separate identities,

15
00:00:48.156 --> 00:00:52.275
because a component that both decides
and acts can cover its tracks.

16
00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:55.275
Second, the host is a control-plane asset.

17
00:00:55.275 --> 00:00:59.333
It reads the forest and
writes to cloud identity,

18
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:04.912
so it's treated as Tier 0: hardened,
and logged centrally under M-26-14.

19
00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:09.112
The program's target posture for
federal production is gated actuation.

20
00:01:09.112 --> 00:01:13.500
The host proposes a correction, and
a person approves it before it runs.

21
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.476
The decision belongs to the
program office, under the steward:

22
00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:21.997
stand up the host as the only
authoritative writer, protected as Tier 0,

23
00:01:21.997 --> 00:01:26.675
and record the standby model and the
actuation stage in the decision log.

24
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:30.620
Gate G0 needs it operational
by the end of Phase 0.
